@startuml agent-state-machine
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Task lifecycle across runs
caption Delivery mode selects PR with human review, PR without it, or guarded direct push to main. Restart entry is delegated to process-restart-recovery.puml.

state "Task scheduler\nIntake, claim, volume/clone, credential-ready container, start update\nSee task-intake.puml and task-scheduler.puml" as Scheduler
state "Executing task run" as Running {
  state "Preflight\nTicket + design + current code\nSee preflight.puml" as Preflight
  state "Implement / validate / review\nSee implementation-review.puml" as Work
  state "Configured delivery\nPR or direct main push\nSee publication.puml" as Publish
  state "Dependency handoff\nPreserve code + create/link ticket\nSee dependency-handoff.puml" as Handoff
  [*] --> Preflight
  Preflight --> Work : ready + prerequisites verified;\n[no pending delivery response/recovery]
  Preflight --> Publish : [publication_resume];\ncurrent task + remote state rechecked
  Work --> Publish : approved exact snapshot\nand required checks passed
  Preflight --> Handoff : necessary work outside scope
  Work --> Handoff : necessary work outside scope
  Work --> Preflight : workspace inputs or target changed\n/ recheck before code assignment
  Publish --> Work : code/base changed or\nnew in-scope review feedback
  Publish --> Handoff : confirmed necessary scope expansion
}
state "Close role sessions\nAll outcomes; stop/fence every executor\nSee role-session.puml: end_run" as CloseSessions
state "Retire or retain run volume\nSystem verifies safe removal or records recovery block\nSee project-workspace.puml: end_run" as CloseWorkspace
state "Synchronize task/Jira outcome\nVerify stage updates or report attention/cancellation\nSee run-outcome-tracking.puml" as OutcomeSync
state "Close run\nPersist outcome + volume recovery references\nRelease active run lease and execution slot" as CloseRun
state Outcome <<choice>>
state "Awaiting human PR review\nNo run, agents, or slot held" as ReviewPending
state "Complete\nTarget branch updated; task status verified\nJira Done if ticket linked" as Complete <<success>>
state "Closed without code\nJira ticket or prompt task marked unneeded" as Unnecessary <<success>>
state "Blocked on prerequisite\nOld run ended; branch preserved" as Blocked <<blocked>>
state "Needs attention\nClarification, policy, budget,\nor incomplete recovery" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Cancelled\nPartial effects remain recorded" as Cancelled <<attention>>

[*] --> Scheduler
Scheduler --> Running : repository/volume clone + current credential verified;\nrun claimed, slot held, task start update verified
Scheduler --> Attention : intake, config, or start update failure
Scheduler --> Cancelled : cancel before dispatch
Preflight --> CloseSessions : unneeded explanation + applicable\ntask/ticket closure confirmed / outcome = no_work
Preflight --> CloseSessions : unresolved evidence\n/ outcome = attention
Work --> CloseSessions : session/workspace/repair needs attention\n/ outcome = attention
Publish --> CloseSessions : [pr_human] PR linked + human\nreview requested / outcome = awaiting_review
Publish --> CloseSessions : PR merged or direct main push verified;\ntask complete / outcome = complete
Publish --> CloseSessions : final human rejection or unresolved review\n/ outcome = attention
Handoff --> CloseSessions : handoff fully confirmed\n/ outcome = dependency_blocked
Handoff --> CloseSessions : recovery cannot finish\n/ outcome = attention
Running --> CloseSessions : unresolvable policy block, exhausted budget,\nor unrecoverable operation / outcome = attention
Running --> CloseSessions : cancellation requested\n/ outcome = cancelled
CloseSessions --> CloseWorkspace : sessions_closed; all executors stopped/fenced
CloseWorkspace --> OutcomeSync : volume_retired or safely retained;\nrecord any task-owned recovery block
OutcomeSync --> CloseRun : tracking_synced / preserve requested outcome
OutcomeSync --> CloseRun : tracking_pending / outcome = attention;\nrecord Jira sync failure and recovery action
CloseRun --> Outcome : outcome persisted; claims + slot released
Outcome --> ReviewPending : [awaiting_review]
Outcome --> Complete : [complete]
Outcome --> Unnecessary : [no_work]
Outcome --> Blocked : [dependency_blocked]
Outcome --> Attention : [attention]
Outcome --> Cancelled : [cancelled]
Blocked --> [*]
Attention --> [*]
ReviewPending --> Scheduler : authenticated PR review or task chat reply\n/ record decision; enqueue NEW run
Complete --> [*]
Unnecessary --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Scheduler
  Jira ticket retrieval and prompt clarification
  are detailed in task-intake.puml.
  Queue admission, the 1-3 limit, atomic claim,
  container credential pull and verified work-start
  update are detailed
  in task-scheduler.puml.
  On process restart, process-restart-recovery.puml
  runs before dispatch. It may restore a waiting task or
  resume an active run at its verified saved stage.
end note
note right of ReviewPending
  Only the pr_human mode enters this state.
  A human response names the task, PR and reviewed commit.
  Changes requested return to implementation after preflight.
  Approval permits merge only after freshness and policy checks.
  Silence never counts as approval.
end note
note right of Running
  Every protected command uses the guardrail and
  delivery submachine in operation-guardrails.puml.
  JSON assignments/results/events are journaled.
  Log messages, handoffs, tools, policy decisions,
  model identity, token usage, and state revisions.
  Operational retries stay within the same operation;
  they do not restart this whole task run.
end note
note right of CloseSessions
  Cleanup failure stays visible here and retains the slot.
  Retry/fencing is detailed in role-session.puml.
  No-code runs safely close without creating role sessions.
end note
note right of OutcomeSync
  A failed Jira outcome update is visible in the task record.
  Cleanup still releases a fenced run's slot after persisting
  an attention outcome; no false Jira success is reported.
end note
note right of CloseWorkspace
  Clean runs can remove the local checkout and keep branch history.
  Dirty work is retained with a complete recovery manifest.
  A retained task volume blocks a new run until reconciled.
  Uncertain cleanup keeps the claim/slot until reconciled.
end note
note right of Blocked
  No agent waits here and no slot is retained.
  The prerequisite is a separate scheduled task.
  Ticket closure alone does not prove its fix landed.
  Resolution may queue a NEW run at the top.
  The next run repeats preflight and uses new sessions.
end note
legend bottom
  Green: successful terminal outcome | Amber: review wait/attention/cancellation | Red: dependency block
  Labels describe events and guards. Only the workflow changes authoritative state.
endlegend
@enduml
